+      <dl newline="true" spacing="normal" indent="3" pn="section-2-1">
+        <dt pn="section-2-1.1">IAC WILL TUID</dt>
+        <dd pn="section-2-1.2">The sender (the TELNET user) proposes to authenticate the user and
+send the identifing UUID; or, the sender (the TELNET user) agrees
+to authenticate the user on whose behalf the connection is
+initiated.</dd>
+        <dt pn="section-2-1.3">IAC WON'T TUID</dt>
+        <dd pn="section-2-1.4">The sender (the TELNET user) refuses to authenticate the user on
+whose behalf the connection is initiated.</dd>
+        <dt pn="section-2-1.5">IAC DO TUID</dt>
+        <dd pn="section-2-1.6">The sender (the TELNET server) proposes that the recipient (the
+TELNET user) authenticate the user and send the identifing UUID;
+or, the sender (the TELNET server) agrees to accept the
+recipient's (the TELNET user's) authentication of the user
+identified by his UUID.</dd>
+        <dt pn="section-2-1.7">IAC DON'T TUID</dt>
+        <dd pn="section-2-1.8">The sender (the TELNET server) refuses to accept the recipient's
+(the TELNET user) authentication of the user.</dd>
+        <dt pn="section-2-1.9">IAC SB TUID &lt;uuid&gt; IAC SE</dt>
+        <dd pn="section-2-1.10">The sender (the TELNET user) sends the UUID &lt;uuid&gt; of the user on
+whose behalf the connection is established to the host to which he
+is connected.  The &lt;uuid&gt; is a 32 bit binary number.</dd>
+      </dl>
